{
  "name": "Competitor Price & Inventory Tracking Sentinel",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. WATCHLIST-DRIVEN SCAN\nEvery 2 hours, pulls the competitor watchlist (competitor, product URL, our matching SKU, and the CSS selectors for that site's price/stock/shipping) and loops through it one row at a time.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "e745030d-ba19-4ef9-9f6d-078395d02b90",
      "name": "Note: ## 1. WATCHLIST-DRIV",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1728,
        176
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. SCRAPE + NORMALIZE\nFetches the live page, extracts price/stock/shipping text with CSS selectors, and a Code node cleans that into real numbers and a clean in-stock boolean.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "99b65b78-7b65-406b-a9d8-0a30ee56c75d",
      "name": "Note: ## 2. SCRAPE + NORMA",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1120,
        192
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. VARIANCE LOGIC\nPulls this SKU's last logged snapshot and compares: price drop ≥10%, or a switch from in-stock to out-of-stock, both count as a market opportunity. Every scrape is logged either way — this is what makes the history queryable for the digest.",
        "height": 416,
        "width": 1632,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "9bb47cc5-0fc5-43c0-bcab-c9ccbaf71f58",
      "name": "Note: ## 3. VARIANCE LOGIC",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -608,
        224
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. INSTANT ALERT\nA flagged opportunity fires a Slack alert immediately, not batched — this is the 'stock just ran out' signal a client wants in minutes, not next morning.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "cb2db294-92f1-4cb1-bdc0-a9c1413c9df1",
      "name": "Note: ## 4. INSTANT ALERT\n",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -16,
        -192
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. MORNING DIGEST (separate trigger)\nA second, independent schedule (8am daily) queries everything flagged in the last 24h from the same history table and sends one rollup message — for clients who want a daily summary instead of a stream of pings.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "8d7997c1-e091-49a5-b83e-f2c07973ba0e",
      "name": "Note: ## 5. MORNING DIGEST",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1728,
        816
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ERROR HANDLING\nAny scrape/API failure fires this Error Trigger and pings ops — a broken competitor selector never fails silently.",
        "height": 308,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "be8d3fe5-d2fe-4b70-9f30-f6613b175293",
      "name": "Note: ## ERROR HANDLING\nAn",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1728,
        1296
      ]
    },
